<title>INDONESIA: Berlian proposes stock split, bonus issue.</title>
<headline>Berlian proposes stock split, bonus issue.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian shipping firm PT Berlian Laju Tanker said on Thursday it planned to increase the number of shares on the market with a stock split and issue bonus shares.</p>
<p>It said in a statement to the Jakarta stock exchange that the plan was subject to shareholder approval at an extraordinary general meeting on November 1.</p>
<p>The company said the nominal value of its shares would be reduced to 500 rupiah from 1,000 rupiah but did not give further details.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
